    <exercise number="">
        <title>Question 6.I</title>
        <statement>
            <p>Consider the first order system:</p>
            <md>
                <mrow>\frac{dx}{dt} \amp= x+y^2</mrow>
                <mrow>\frac{dy}{dt} \amp= xy</mrow>
            </md>
            <p>with initial conditions of <m>x(0)=1</m> and <m>y(0)=-1</m>. Use Modified Euler with <m>\Delta t = 0.2</m> to approximate the solution to this system from <m>t=0</m> to <m>t=2</m>. Please validate your solution with <c>ode23</c> and reflect on any specifics regarding your results.</p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise number="">
        <title>Question 6.J</title>
        <statement>
            <p>Consider the first order system:</p>
            <md>
                <mrow>\frac{dx}{dt} \amp= t+y^2</mrow>
                <mrow>\frac{dy}{dt} \amp= x-y</mrow>
            </md>
            <p>with initial conditions of <m>x(0)=2</m> and <m>y(0)=-1</m>. Compute two steps of Modified Euler with <m>\Delta t = 0.2</m> to approximate the solution to this system.</p>
        </statement>
        <solution>
            <p>The work can be shown via Matlab below, but can be done via calculator. The important thing is to store as much into calculator memory as possible.</p>
            <program language="matlab">
                <input><![CDATA[
                % Initialize everything
                >> f = @(t,x,y)[t+y.^2; x-y]; t0 = 0; w0 = [2; -1]; h=0.2;
                >> m1 = f(t0, w0(1), w0(2))
                m1 =
                     1
                     3
                ]]></input>
                
                <input><![CDATA[
                >> alpha = w0+h*m1; % update of w for m2
                >> m2 = f(t0+h,alpha(1),alpha(2))
                m2 =
                   0.560000000000000
                   2.600000000000000
                ]]></input>
                <input><![CDATA[
                >> w1 = w0 + (h/2)*(m1+m2)
                w1 =
                   2.156000000000000
                  -0.440000000000000
                ]]></input>
                <input><![CDATA[
                >> t1 = t0+h;
                >> m1 = f(t1,w1(1),w1(2))
                m1 =
                   0.393600000000000
                   2.596000000000000
                ]]></input>
                <input><![CDATA[
                >> alpha = w1+h*m1; % update of w for m2
                >> m2 = f(t1+h,alpha(1),alpha(2))
                m2 =
                   0.406272640000000
                   2.155520000000000
                ]]></input>
                <input><![CDATA[
                >> w2 = w1 + (h/2)*(m1+m2)
                 w2 =
                   2.235987264000000
                   0.035152000000000
                ]]></input>
            </program>
        </solution>
    </exercise>

    
</exercises>
